---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Our farm" description="See how Vermicompost Farm turns prepared organic matter into living black gold in Pretoria.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Our farm" title="Small farm. Millions of workers." intro="Red wigglers quietly turn local organic material into healthier soil." image="/farm/windrows.jpg" />
  <section class="section"><div class="container story"><div><p class="eyebrow">Made in Montana, Pretoria</p><h2>We let nature do the complicated part.</h2></div><div><p class="lede">Vermicompost Farm produces castings made by red wigglers—Eisenia fetida—with a small amount of stable organic matter.</p><p>Horse manure and wood shavings are prepared before being fed to the worms. Over roughly ten weeks, they become nutrient-rich vermicast: a natural soil conditioner gardeners often call black gold.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="process"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">From organic matter to vermicompost</p><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><h3>Prepare</h3><p>Local organic material is pre-composted until it is ready for the worms.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Let the worms work</h3><p>Red wigglers transform it into stable, microbe-rich castings.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Sift</h3><p>The finished compost is sifted into a fine, useful soil conditioner.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section gallery-section"><div class="container gallery"><figure class="large"><img src="/farm/worm-bins-open.jpg" alt="Open worm production bins" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The working worm beds</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/farm/red-wigglers.jpg" alt="Red wiggler worms in bedding" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Eisenia fetida</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/farm/trommel-sifter.jpg" alt="Trommel sifter used on the farm" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Fine sifting</figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="visit"><div class="container"><div><p class="eyebrow">See it for yourself</p><h2>Visit the working farm.</h2></div><a class="button button--paper" href="/visit">Plan a visit</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(42px, 8vw, 100px); }.story h2 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 4.6rem); }.story p:not(.lede) { color: var(--muted); }
  .process { padding: 52px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--white); }.steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 20px; }.steps article { padding: 24px 30px; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }.steps article:first-child { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }.steps span { color: var(--clay); font-family: var(--serif); }.steps h3 { margin: 22px 0 8px; }.steps p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; }
  .gallery { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr .75fr; grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }.gallery figure { position: relative; min-height: 230px; margin: 0; overflow: hidden; }.gallery .large { grid-row: 1/3; }.gallery img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; filter: saturate(.8); }.gallery figcaption { position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--paper); color: var(--soil); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: .9rem; }
  .visit { padding: 62px 0; background: var(--green-dark); color: var(--white); }.visit .container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: end; gap: 30px; }.visit .eyebrow { color: #d5dfd1; }.visit h2 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .story, .steps, .gallery { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.steps article, .steps article:first-child { padding: 22px 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }.gallery { grid-template-rows: auto; }.gallery .large { grid-row: auto; }.gallery figure { min-height: 260px; }.visit .container { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
